Implementation Plan - Quran Verse Reminders
This plan introduces a feature allowing users to set up a reminder with a specific Quran verse (Ayah). When the scheduled time is reached, the application will:

Trigger a local notification with the verse details.
Natively play the verse audio.
If the app is in the foreground, display a beautiful, premium overlay dialog with the Arabic text of the verse and playback controls.
User Review Required
NOTE

Reminders will now be persistent using a Hive box (reminders_box) instead of mock in-memory lists, making the reminder feature fully functional.

Proposed Changes
1. Data Model & Repository Layer
[MODIFY] 
reminder_model.dart
Update ReminderModel to support Quran-related fields:
bool isQuranReminder
int? surahNumber
String? surahName
int? ayahNumber
String? ayahText
String? audioUrl
Update ReminderModelAdapter to read and write fields 4 through 9 for Hive storage, ensuring backward compatibility.
[MODIFY] 
quran_repository.dart
Add a fetchAyah(int surahNumber, int ayahNumber) method to query /ayah/$surahNumber:$ayahNumber/ar.alafasy from the Alquran API to retrieve the verse text and audio URL.
2. State & Scheduling Layer
[MODIFY] 
app_router.dart
Make _rootNavigatorKey a public top-level variable rootNavigatorKey so it can be accessed by the scheduler to display foreground dialogs.
[MODIFY] 
reminder_provider.dart
Update ReminderNotifier to open reminders_box and fetch, add, update, and delete reminders to/from Hive.
Add deleteReminder(String id).
Implement reminderSchedulerProvider which initializes a Timer.periodic checking every 10 seconds:
Finds any enabled reminder where scheduledTime is in the past.
Automatically toggles it to disabled.
Shows a local notification with the verse info.
If a Quran reminder is triggered, plays the ayah audio.
If the app is in the foreground, opens a dialog displaying the Arabic verse text, surah name, translation, and media play/pause controls.
3. UI Screens
